From: Sanjay Ravindran <mail2snjyrvndrn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: mr7500: fix AQR114C USXGMII probe race, LED hw control, and SSDK AN

- Serialize phy_attach_direct() with phy_probe() via device_lock(d) (0984) so
  qca-nss-dp does not attach wan before AQR114C firmware upload finishes.
- Guard phy_led_hw_control_get_device() and netdev_trig_activate() against
  unregistered netdevs whose dev_name() is NULL before register_netdev() (0985).
- Enable PHYXS USXGMII Clause 37 in-band auto-neg in aquantia_main (0983) and
  increase SSDK UNIPHY USXGMII autoneg poll retries (001).
- Fix linksys,mr7500 5GbE WAN LED sysfs path (green:wan) and omit unsupported
  link_10 so AQR114C hardware LED offload activates.

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq60xx/base-files/etc/board.d/01_leds b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq60xx/base-files/etc/board.d/01_leds
index 2f39503..90814ef 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq60xx/base-files/etc/board.d/01_leds
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq60xx/base-files/etc/board.d/01_leds
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@ linksys,mr7500)
 	ucidef_set_led_netdev "lan3-port-traffic" "LAN3-PORT-TRAFFIC" "90000.mdio-1:02:orange:lan" "lan3" "tx rx link_10 link_100 link_1000"
 	ucidef_set_led_netdev "lan4-port-link" "LAN4-PORT-LINK" "90000.mdio-1:03:green:lan" "lan4" "link_10 link_100 link_1000"
 	ucidef_set_led_netdev "lan4-port-traffic" "LAN4-PORT-TRAFFIC" "90000.mdio-1:03:orange:lan" "lan4" "tx rx link_10 link_100 link_1000"
-	ucidef_set_led_netdev "wan-port-link" "WAN-PORT-LINK" "90000.mdio-1:08:green:lan" "wan" "link_10 link_100 link_1000 link_2500 link_5000"
-	ucidef_set_led_netdev "wan-port-traffic" "WAN-PORT-TRAFFIC" "90000.mdio-1:08:orange:wan" "wan" "tx rx link_10 link_100 link_1000 link_2500 link_5000"
+	ucidef_set_led_netdev "wan-port-link" "WAN-PORT-LINK" "90000.mdio-1:08:green:wan" "wan" "link_100 link_1000 link_2500 link_5000"
+	ucidef_set_led_netdev "wan-port-traffic" "WAN-PORT-TRAFFIC" "90000.mdio-1:08:orange:wan" "wan" "tx rx link_100 link_1000 link_2500 link_5000"
 	;;
 yuncore,fap650)
 	ucidef_set_led_netdev "wlan5ghz" "WLAN 5GHz LED" "blue:wlan-5ghz" "wlan0" "tx rx"
